7. Tollbooth Taxonomy

Physical Tollbooth
Critical equipment, infrastructure, materials, manufacturing stages, ports, transmission networks, or other physical passages.

Design Tollbooth
Tools or intellectual infrastructure required to design complex systems.

Protocol / Standard Tollbooth
Interfaces whose value comes from interoperability or widespread adoption.

Platform Tollbooth
Operating environments through which producers reach users or other systems.

Distribution Tollbooth
Channels connecting production to customers.

Information Tollbooth
Data, indexes, identity systems, verification layers, or information infrastructure required for decisions or transactions.

Financial Tollbooth
Payment, clearing, settlement, exchange, custody, or financing infrastructure.

Regulatory Tollbooth
Certification, licensing, approval, or compliance passages required for participation.

Network Tollbooth
Communication/interconnection layers through which otherwise competing systems must communicate.

Meta-Tollbooth
A Tollbooth whose customers include other Tollbooths.

