9. Critical Distinction: Tollbooth ≠ Good Investment

Finding a Tollbooth solves a structural problem, not a valuation problem.

Great\ Tollbooth
\neq
Great\ Investment

Investment attractiveness additionally requires:

ExpectedReturn
=
f(
TollboothQuality,
Growth,
Price,
Expectations,
CapitalIntensity,
Margins,
Regulation,
Competition,
Execution,
Time
)

Therefore:

\boxed{\text{Find Tollbooth} \rightarrow \text{Assay Tollbooth} \rightarrow \text{Price Tollbooth}}

Never skip the third step.

