11. Leading Indicators

Watch for convergence of previously separate competitors onto the same infrastructure, increasing adoption of a shared standard, rising utilization, growing backlog, increasing switching costs, ecosystem expansion, repeat usage, customer investment around the interface, complementary innovation, competitors integrating rather than bypassing, and evidence that new entrants increase traffic through the incumbent interface.

Especially powerful:

Competitor\ count\uparrow
\quad+\quad
Tollbooth\ traffic\uparrow

If new competitors strengthen rather than weaken the interface controller, the Tollbooth hypothesis gains evidence.

⸻

12. Invalidation

A Tollbooth thesis weakens when:

Dependency\downarrow

or

Substitution\uparrow

or

Capture\downarrow

or

Traffic\downarrow

or

Bypassability\uparrow.

The cleanest invalidation event is:

\boxed{\text{A credible winner succeeds without crossing the supposed Tollbooth.}}

That observation attacks the claimed invariant directly.

